# Form Controls and Pickers

Form controls are part of the product's visual language. They must feel designed, not like OS defaults in an otherwise polished UI.

**Never ship raw native controls as final UI** unless the user explicitly asks for native controls.

## Match the design system

Before building any control, match:

- border radius, border weight, and surfaces used by buttons and cards
- typography scale for labels, helper text, errors
- accent color, focus ring, hover/active, disabled styling
- spacing rhythm and control height with adjacent inputs and buttons

If `components/ui/` primitives exist, use them. Do not create a second visual style.

## All controls

- Custom-styled UI over semantic HTML, or project headless primitives — fully restyled.
- Comfortable mobile hit areas (not 12px targets).
- Polished `hover`, `focus-visible`, `disabled`, `invalid`, `loading` states.
- Preserve keyboard and screen-reader behavior.

## Checkboxes and radios

- No default browser checkbox/radio as visible UI.
- Custom indicators: rounded square/circle, subtle border, accent fill, smooth check/dot transition.
- Clickable labels; consistent group spacing.

## Dropdowns and selects

- No native `<select>` as visible UI.
- Trigger matches text inputs: height, padding, radius, border, background.
- Menu: elevation, border, radius, item padding, hover/selected states.
- Long lists: search/filter + empty state. Multi-select: styled chips/tags.

## Calendars and date/time

- No `<input type="date|time|datetime-local">` as final UI.
- Calendar panel matches design system: navigation, weekdays, today/selected/range/disabled states.
- Styled trigger showing formatted value; handle locale and mobile usability.

## Text fields

- Inputs, textareas, search, number fields share one system with dropdown/date triggers.
- Consistent placeholders, icons, clear buttons, error messaging.
- Combobox/autocomplete matches dropdown styling.

## Avoid

- Gray bordered rectangles unrelated to the page
- Mixed native + custom controls in one form
- Tiny checkboxes beside large polished buttons
- Browser-default calendar popups
- Invisible focus rings

When adding a dependency for primitives, prefer small headless libraries only if none exist — always restyle to match the product.
